      "confidence": "needs_confirmation",
      "program_name": "Affordable Housing and Employee Accommodation Ordinance (County Code Chapter 15.65): 10% inclusionary requirement, in-lieu fee and employee accommodation fee",
      "administering_agency": "Placer County Community Development Resource Agency (entitlement review) and Economic Development and Housing Division (fee collection and use); nexus study update by BAE Urban Economics under a February 4, 2025 contract",
      "funding_type": "density bonus",
      "typical_award_size": "Regulatory requirement and the County's only local housing revenue. Adopted October 2020, effective January 1, 2021: private residential projects of more than 100 units must make 10% of units affordable; projects of 8 to 100 units pay an in-lieu fee per habitable square foot of market-rate units (initially $2.00, indexed, reported at $2.73 on the County's program page); projects of 7 or fewer units and projects in infill or transit areas are exempt. An employee accommodation fee at the same per-square-foot rate applies to new non-residential development in the Sierra Nevada and Lake Tahoe areas. Fees fund construction, preservation and acquisition-rehab of affordable housing. Large specific plans (Bickford Ranch, Placer One) have generated the in-lieu balances now lent to Hope Way and proposed for Destination at Placer One.",
      "per_unit_cap": null,
      "affordability_requirement": "10% of units at affordable levels defined in the ordinance for projects over 100 units, with the in-lieu alternative below that size; state density bonus law applies to projects providing affordable units. The updated nexus study (draft December 2025) supports higher fees and ordinance amendments scheduled for Board consideration in 2026.",
      "eligible_project_types": [
        "new construction",
        "mixed-use",
        "homeownership"
      ],
      "application_cycle": "rolling",
      "next_deadline": "Applies at entitlement (Affordable Housing Employee Accommodation Entitlement Review Form) with fees paid at building permit. Board adoption of the nexus study and fee or ordinance amendments was planned for spring 2026 and was still pending in the records reviewed; confirm the current fee with the Planning Division before underwriting.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "false",
      "layering_notes": "placer.ca.gov (including DocumentCenter PDFs) sits behind Cloudflare and refused automated access on 2026-11-06; Board items were read from the County's GovDelivery agenda attachments (content.govdelivery.com/attachments/CAPLACER), the Legistar client 'placerca', state records and news coverage. For a 100% affordable project the ordinance is not a cost; for a mixed-income project over 100 units it is a 10% set-aside, and between 8 and 100 units a fee of roughly $2.73 per square foot (about $2,700 on a 1,000 square foot unit), which is low relative to Bay Area counties. The fee revenue is the pool behind the County's gap loans, so a higher fee from the 2026 nexus update would expand the only local source. The County's exemptions for infill and transit-adjacent projects remove most of western Placer's multifamily sites from the requirement. Density bonus and inclusionary agreements do not trigger prevailing wage.",
      "source_url": "https://www.publicceo.com/?p=64372",
      "record_id": "cfb800c3eb",
      "cycle_notes": "",
      "eligible_project_detail": [
        "new construction",
        "homeownership",
        "mixed-use"
      ],
      "next_deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_check": "no_date"
    }
