      "program_name": "Permanent Local Housing Allocation (PLHA), Placer County formula allocation",
      "administering_agency": "Placer County Executive Office, Economic Development and Housing Division",
      "funding_type": "grant",
      "typical_award_size": "2019-2023 five-year formula estimate $2,730,542 (Board resolution with a 302(c)(4) plan; HCD awarded $455,090 for the 2019 allocation on October 21, 2020; the County ran a PLHA NOFA for developers in 2020). HCD's 2024-2028 formula NOFA lists Placer County at $489,950 (2024), $538,105 (2025) and an estimated $3,062,188 over five years. Cities receive their own allocations: Roseville about $1.37 million, Rocklin about $591,000, Lincoln about $585,000 and Auburn about $440,000 over five years.",
      "per_unit_cap": null,
      "affordability_requirement": "PLHA guidelines: rental housing at or below 60% AMI (up to 80% AMI) with 55-year covenants, or other activities in the County's five-year plan. The 2024-2028 plan activities and any current County PLHA NOFA could not be opened (placer.ca.gov blocked).",
      "eligible_project_types": [
        "new construction",
        "acquisition-rehab",
        "preservation",
        "supportive housing",
        "homeownership"
      ],
      "application_cycle": "annual NOFA",
      "next_deadline": "The County must adopt a new five-year plan for the 2024-2028 allocations under HCD's amended formula NOFA; no 2026 Board action was found in the records reviewed. Ask the Economic Development and Housing Division whether PLHA will be offered through a NOFA or committed to specific projects.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "true",
      "layering_notes": "placer.ca.gov (including DocumentCenter PDFs) sits behind Cloudflare and refused automated access on 2026-11-06; Board items were read from the County's GovDelivery agenda attachments (content.govdelivery.com/attachments/CAPLACER), the Legistar client 'placerca', state records and news coverage. At about $500,000 a year, County PLHA is a modest deal-specific source and the County has used a competitive NOFA for it before (2020), so a developer can ask for the next cycle to be run the same way. It can also be stacked under the County's in-lieu fee loan on a project like Hope Way. State funds trigger prevailing wage.",
      "source_url": "https://www.hcd.ca.gov/grants-funding/active-funding/plha/docs/PLHA_Program_Awardee_List.pdf",
